<title>FRANCE: Moulinex sees oper results improving.</title>
<headline>Moulinex sees oper results improving.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Appliance manufacturer Moulinex said in a prospectus for a capital increase that it expected its operating result for 1996/97 to be higher than the 54 million franc operating profit recorded for 1995/96.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite the sluggishness of the European market, the efforts to restore a normal level of industrial activity and favourable trends in raw materials prices point to an operating result superior to last year's,&quot; it said. It also said it had introduced short-time working to reduce inventories.</p>
<p>Moulinex has set a 525 million franc capital increase.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
